non-linear-change-8f9e8ad1.limits_and_boundary:
In regions where the electromagnetic field strength 
 F_{μν}
 approaches zero (i.e., in regions of vanishing electromagnetic fields), the commutator of the covariant derivatives also approaches zero. This means that in such regions, the covariant derivatives commute, behaving like ordinary partial derivatives. This limit corresponds to free particles not interacting with any electromagnetic fields. As the field strength 
 F_{μν}
 becomes very large, the non-commutativity of the covariant derivatives becomes significant, indicating strong electromagnetic interactions.
